 ## Rental service
 
 `createRentalService()` creates an isolated in-memory rental service. Register each board or sail with
-`addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })`, where money is an integer number of euro cents. `quote()`
-prices a request and `book()` reserves it; both accept `{ itemId, start, end }` and require UTC
-ISO-8601 timestamps at midnight. Rental periods are start-inclusive and end-exclusive, so the end is
-the midnight following the final rental day. A booking cannot overlap an existing booking for the same
-item. `availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns sorted IDs of equipment without an overlapping
-booking for that full period, optionally restricted to `board` or `sail`. Cancellation is not
-implemented yet. Rentals of three or more days receive a 10% discount on the full price, rounded to
-the nearest euro cent; both `quote()` and `book()` return this reduced total.
+`addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice, hourlyPrice? })`, where money is an integer number of euro
+cents. `quote()` prices a request and `book()` reserves it; both accept `{ itemId, start, end }`.
+Daily rentals require UTC ISO-8601 timestamps at midnight and are start-inclusive and end-exclusive,
+so the end is the midnight following the final rental day. Rentals shorter than one day may start and
+end on exact UTC hours; they cost `hourlyPrice` for each hour, and require that price to be configured
+on the equipment. A booking cannot overlap an existing booking for the same item.
+`availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns sorted IDs of equipment without an overlapping booking
+for a full-day period, optionally restricted to `board` or `sail`. Cancellation is not implemented
+yet. Rentals of three or more days receive a 10% discount on the full price, rounded to the nearest
+euro cent; both `quote()` and `book()` return this reduced total.
